README for 2026-08-04 primary elections.

I. Finding, getting, and storing the data from the county election reports.

   1. Tracking the data.
      The tracking spreadsheet for the primary election data is at:
      https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1tQl_3ekd6uBhWYle5eNGthreMqoJj8LS7ARjkUaDkkM/edit?gid=158379855#gid=158379855

      Green bars are 1st priority counties; yellow bars are 2nd priority.  Everything else is 3rd priority.

   2. Recording county clerk election pages.
      This time around, we're saving the page that, in turn, points to the actual primary election results URL.
      This way, come November, we can (presumably) start from THAT page, to find the general election results
      URL.

   3. Actual election results.
      We have several 'flavors' of election results URLs, which are in turn indicated by the "page type"
      column:
         Vendor Page (w/ Result)  -- the vendor page (notably EnhancedVoting) that in turn contains
                                     results for multiple elections.  Our download scripts start from
                                     there to get the final, machine-readable, result (usually JSON).

         Vendor Page (NO Results) -- same as above, except there are NO results for this election there (yet).
       
         ACTUAL Results           -- the URL of the actual results, typically a PDF file.

   4. Getting the data.
      The actual method of downloading the data depends on the data format:

      Enhanced voting.  

   4. Saving the data.
      The election results files are stored in the ElectionImport project, PRIMARIES directory.  We use the
      same filename format as before, e.g. 11-berrien_2026-08-04.json.ph1.json or
      70-ottawa_2026-08-04.clarity.ph1.csv


